 "_us_estimate_note": "DOMESTIC labelled estimates, added 2026-08-14. DOT's Consumer Airfare Report only covers city pairs averaging at least 10 passengers a day, so it publishes nothing for Nantucket, Aspen, Jackson Hole, Key West, Destin and the rest of the small leisure markets — which are exactly the destinations this account exists to show. Unlike dot_round_trip and intl_estimate_round_trip, the number here is the TYPICAL CHEAP ROUND TRIP itself, not an annual average, so seed_baselines applies NO cheap-fare factor to it. Every route seeded this way carries basis ESTIMATE and must stay labelled as an estimate wherever it is shown.",
 "leisure_pool": {
  "_doc": [
   "The destination list, 2026-08-14 (owner's call). This is the ranked leisure list,",
   "minus Wilmington, Hilton Head and Charleston. It REPLACES 'every city pair DOT",
   "publishes' as the thing the board draws from.",
   "",
   "Adopting every DOT pair was the right way to get real fare baselines and the wrong",
   "way to pick holidays: DOT publishes what people fly, and what people fly is largely",
   "work. It put Wichita, Des Moines, Rochester, Hartford and Buffalo on a travel account",
   "while missing Key West, Nantucket, Aspen and Jackson Hole.",
   "",
   "tier drives EXPOSURE, not eligibility. See config/tiers.json."
  ],
